C01a adds a pure policy core with nine tests. Independent review found that the original review names an older harness than the executed composition. The core now refuses that unchanged historical packet. Coherent positive policy fixtures are explicitly synthetic. C01b performs actual current file/Git inspection, requiring exactly nine JARs and five class files. Its actual CLI refuses the old packet and admits only current retained-input consistency under a new separately scoped review. Seventeen tests passed; a test-only Clippy lint was repaired, then only that affected test and fmt/Clippy were rerun. Both captures are retained. No native execution was replayed for these tools; current inspection proves neither historical dependency immutability nor publisher authenticity.

