Parent **C01 and C03 remain open**, with all original tasks required and downstream gates retained. These child tools do not establish exact rebuilt-artifact equivalence, full inherited capability inventory, landing closure or UI/UX/performance acceptance. Existing held model/factory/initializer paths and canonical dirty work are preserved. No merge or deployment occurred. [Execution ledger](execution.json), [publication identities](published-prs.json) and [current validation](batch3-validation.json) retain the bounded evidence.


## Fourth independent batch

The graph after the fourth batch contained **727 review units and 1,454 acyclic readiness nodes**, with no unordered source-write conflicts. Added named C01c/C01d/C03b children before implementation dispatch. These are review scopes, not a feature count or completion percentage. The original 33/47 accounting and prior planning/validation captures remain unchanged.

Three separate two-commit drafts are published: [C01d #79](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/79), [C01c #80](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/80) and [C03b #81](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/81). C01c/C01d independently target the frozen integration head. C03b targets an exact snapshot containing #71–#75: 130 selected files plus one ordered generated export. Land reviewed prerequisites, retarget, inspect and revalidate; never merge into temporary snapshots.

C01c captures the actual anonymous native GraphQL contract: 671 types, 1,418 fields, 809 input fields and seven directive definitions. The unchanged native guard rejected the initial combined capability probe; five bounded single-type requests plus full introspection succeed in a fresh epoch. The CLI preserves the full schema Value, exact defaults and member-array order, validates complete references and streams compact output. Ten reader tests and eight final actual CLI cases pass. Failed helper cases, later CLI-only checks and the native refusal remain distinct. All 46 loaded SDL resources match selected pinned source bytes; the source-only forkstudio resource was not loaded in this artifact/configuration.

C01d captures the actual applied PostgreSQL contract: 15 tables, 87 columns, 26 constraints, 16 indexes and 20 applied migrations. Its Rust projection preserves all 164 descriptors and execution order, checks complete FK/backing-index references, and stops output amplification with incremental byte accounting. Ten tests and five actual CLI cases pass. The shared first native receipt remains PARTIAL because its independent GraphQL probe failed; only the successful catalog is credited here, and it was not replayed. All 29 shipped DB XML resources match selected pinned Sirius source bytes. The reviewed cohesive 520-production/1050-authored exception includes the final 518/1042 lines of implementation, tests, SQL and manifest; shared execution evidence is a separate review block.

C03b connects actual semantic cleanup, Document admission, B01 library-ID preparation and B25d control-description migration in one private project-preparation API. It validates every selected watermark before resolver work and retains authoritative wire JSON for namespace eligibility and replay. Ten integration tests and 36 tests on the four-module snapshot pass. New native-segment projects match complete JSON values and first namespace keys; a late failure retains native partial mutation while Rust publishes no partial project. The original stdout Unicode mismatch and corrected UTF-8 capture are retained without text normalization. This comparison keeps B01 active with local, nonmatching library references and does not claim native B01 history/library-ID equivalence.

Release measurements cover 256/1024/4096 synthetic semantic nodes plus six diagram nodes. Median preparation is 1.77/6.89/29.10 ms, p95 is 2.25/6.92/29.31 ms, and whole-observer peak RSS is 5,184/11,328/37,612 KiB. Each process discards two warmups and retains ten raw measured samples. Preparation timing excludes decoding/encoding; RSS includes the entire observer. No native performance ratio, general capacity or UI responsiveness is established.

Parent **C01 and C03 remain open**. The official artifact label still differs from target source by 125 paths; exact independent build, remaining inherited/effective ownership, resolver/auth/action behavior, full DB/transaction/durability and connected UI acceptance remain required. Every new unit remains NOT_ACCEPTED for full feature parity. Held paths and canonical dirty work are preserved; nothing merged or deployed. See [execution](execution.json), [publication identities](published-prs.json) and [current gate validation](batch4-validation.json).


