C01e derives the exact 125-path label-to-target delta into seven Java class families, 114 SVG resources and four documentation-only exclusions. The coordinator compiled only the seven explicit target sources against 312 identified native JARs, disabled annotation/implicit processing, and consumed the actual Rust recipe to create a separately named comparison artifact. Only three nested JAR payloads change; 309 remain byte-identical. Full readback preserves unselected payloads and declared ZIP metadata, with physical offsets/compressed lengths recorded separately. The empty BOOT.SF marker is preserved by an exact zero-byte exception; cryptographic signatures and manifest digests refuse. The reviewed cohesive size exception is 475 production/900 authored lines; implementation is 469/820.

Nine original tests and the independently identified versioned-SVG shadow regression pass in separate attributed stages, with formatting, Clippy and CLI builds. The final recipe is byte-identical to the consumed recipe. Twenty-six actual native icon/style provider cases pass. A fresh derived application/owned PostgreSQL epoch serves all 114 SVGs with exact target Git bytes and passes two read-only GraphQL queries, then stops all owned processes. Original prototype import/expectation failures and partial observations remain retained. This is a source-delta-derived comparison artifact, not an independent whole Maven/frontend source build or whole-artifact source binding. Rendered UI, usability and capacity acceptance remain open.

C01f captures the actual 54 dispatcher rows, 33 structured MVC mappings, five filters and one servlet plus 22 fixed anonymous wire probes. Complete mapping trees, repeated header pairs and exact entity bodies are preserved. Nine native HTTP 200 observations contain the same 504-byte frontend HTML shell; they are not API successes. Independent review and actual CLI comparison found numeric precision loss; the existing serde_json arbitrary_precision feature fixes large opaque integers and captured decimal values without adding registry versions. All eleven tests pass after that change; a later anonymous-context consistency guard passes its affected test and final formatting/Clippy/build. Seven final CLI cases preserve both native payload values exactly and verify manifest bytes/refusals. Original lint and precision failures retain their exact attribution. General Rust HTTP/controller/auth/action/streaming behavior remains open.

C03c encodes only an actual prepared project using its authoritative wire JSON and all six nullable stamp families. Inline RawValue keeps payload token bytes, namespace order, large integers and opaque content; strict local-envelope metadata refuses missing/duplicate/unknown/future fields. Decode returns untrusted input for real preparation. Nine roundtrip/admission/boundary tests, one compile-fail API test, formatting and Clippy pass with unchanged registry tuples. The inherited fixture's supplemental Git binding is explicitly separate from the original capture. Native project archive format, durable SQL/publication and timing/capacity claims remain open.

Independent source reviews pass; exact inputs match committed blobs. Parent **C01/C03 and all application/UI/release acceptance gates remain open**. [Execution](execution.json), [publication identities](published-prs.json) and [batch verification](batch5-validation.json) record the bounded results.


## Sixth independent batch

The graph now contains **733 review units and 1,466 readiness nodes**. C01g/C01h/C02a were registered before parallel source dispatch with disjoint isolated ownership. The library catalogue is an explicit M15 prerequisite and the template contract is a B23 prerequisite. All existing dependencies remain; parent C01/C02 and full application acceptance stay open. Review counts are not feature-completion percentages.

Separate two-commit drafts: [C01g](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/85), [C02a](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/86) and [C01h](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/87). Each targets frozen integration. Source authors held no compiler/native lifecycle lease; the coordinator serialized offline builds and native epochs. Independent source reviews pass, committed inputs match captures, held paths and canonical dirty work are preserved. Nothing merged or deployed.

C01g builds an atomic Rust physical catalogue over actual standard-library JSON, preserving raw bytes and separating resource-scoped node IDs from semantic IDs without fallback or a second semantic engine. Its independent limits fit all 94 shipped files (20,874,941 bytes, depth208) without changing project limits. Nine tests, formatting, Clippy and debug/release builds pass. A real native default-configuration observer uses the actual Boot classpath order; all 109,673 stored identity/class/name tuples match through a keyed comparison. This does not qualify native traversal order, fragment aliases or resolved references. A single full release CLI process takes0.34s wall and150,928KiB peak RSS including49MB index serialization; no median/p95/native ratio or SLA is inferred. A reviewed cohesive450-production/900-authored exception retains allocation and filesystem guards; implementation is450 production lines.

The native configuration also reports12,162 PackageNotFound diagnostics and zero warnings. A separate diagnostic-only epoch captures previously missing message/location/type details while retaining the original node observation. These are observed diagnostics, not proof of current unresolved-reference counts or general deployed application failure. Namespace roots and library packages exhibit distinct semantic-fragment lookup behavior. M15/M16, full loading/resolution, caller/UI/capacity acceptance and independent source-build binding remain open. Large corpus/native/index bytes stay externally hash-addressed; genuine small fixtures and compact metadata are committed.

